🎉 Success Checklist
[ ] ChromaDB container running (green status)
[ ] Sample content processed (6+ documents)
[ ] Web app accessible at localhost:3000
[ ] Chapter summary page shows connected status
[ ] Can generate summaries with sample data
[ ] PDFs converted to text files
[ ] Real content processed successfully
[ ] Can generate summaries with your content
🆘 Quick Help
If anything goes wrong:
Run: npm run docker:status (check ChromaDB)
Run: npm run convert-help (check files)
Look at: SYSTEM_STATUS_FIXED.md (full docs)
Your system is ready to use! 🎉
Just follow these steps in order, and you'll have a fully working educational AI system processing your content in under 10 minutes.



npm run docker:start

npm run ingest

npm run dev

Step 5: Convert Your PDFs to Text

    # Install PDF tools (one time only)
    sudo apt-get install poppler-utils  # Linux
    # or: brew install poppler           # Mac

    # Convert your PDFs
    cd app/samples
    pdftotext "Chapter 1.pdf" "chapter1.txt"
    pdftotext "Testbank Chapter (1).pdf" "testbank.txt"
    cd ../..


# Your files should be here:
ls app/samples/
# Should show: chapter1.txt, testbank.txt (plus the PDFs)


Step 7: Process Your Real Content
npm run ingest

🔧 Phase 3: Troubleshooting & Management
npm run docker:status


//////////////
Common Issues & Fixes
Issue: "Port already allocated"

npm run docker:clean
npm run docker:start


Issue: "No documents found"

# Check files exist:
ls app/samples/*.txt

# Re-run ingestion:
npm run ingest


Issue: "ChromaDB not responding"
npm run docker:restart



Issue: Need help with PDF conversion
npm run convert-help


Stop Everything When Done

# Stop web app: Ctrl+C in the terminal
# Stop ChromaDB:
npm run docker:stop


🎯 Complete Command Reference

npm run docker:start    # Start ChromaDB
npm run ingest          # Process content  
npm run dev             # Start web app



Managing Content:
npm run convert-help    # PDF conversion guide
npm run ingest          # Process new content


Docker Management:
npm run docker:status   # Check if running
npm run docker:stop     # Stop ChromaDB
npm run docker:clean    # Fix conflicts
npm run docker:restart  # Restart everything



